<p><strong>Postmark:</strong> Buena Vista, Colorado, 6 PM, 30 December 1913</p>

<p><strong>Addressed to:</strong><br>
Mrs. Annie Fry<br>
518 E First St<br>
Trinidad, Colo.</p>

<p><strong>Message:</strong></p>
<blockquote>Dear Mama I hope you had a Merry Christmas and I wish you a Happy New Year. Why don't you write. With lots of love, Maude</blockquote>

<p>Written upside-down at the top of the card, referring to the photograph on the front:</p>
<blockquote>This is near were [sic] we live now.</blockquote>

<figure class="source-doc-image">
  <img src="/images/site/maude-postcard-front-1913.jpg" alt="Sepia-toned photograph postcard of Chalk Creek Canyon near St. Elmo, Colorado, showing a narrow canyon with steep rocky walls and scattered pine trees along a creek bed.">
  <figcaption>"Chalk Creek Cañon near St. Elmo, Colo." — the photograph Maud references in her upside-down note. Hartley 125.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p>St. Elmo is now a ghost town.</p>